hasDescription.value_text:
locally published book with stories and photos by local residents; on cover and inside back of title page: photo of Martha hachmeister Cherry taken by Herman Hachmeister, her father, 1918; caption reads "Martha Hachmeister Cherry, a Fish Creek "resorter," living it up on vacation in the summer of 1918; Martha's first encounter with Door County was staying with her family at Herman Welker's resort in Fish Creek (where Herman Hachmeister met William Bernhard); see also photo of Martha on vehicle with other children;
Physical Description: 8.5 x 5.5 
286 pages with photos and index
